flags: --optimize whole

--- OUT --->
28
--- IR --->
// **the whole of the assertion is the region between these two lines.** the parameter and
// `local_unnamed_addr` are what make the first one the *definition* rather than the call site in `main`,
// and a CHECK-NOT is scoped between its neighbours - which it has to be here, since `mem::` declares
// `@malloc` and half the standard library calls it somewhere above this
CHECK: i64 @_accumulateZZMLPl(i64 %seed) local_unnamed_addr

// no block, so nothing to give back and nothing to copy between two of them. the `memcpy` is the one
// that would come back first if the argument were duplicated again: two blocks each read by the other
// are two allocations neither of which is dead
CHECK-NOT: @malloc
CHECK-NOT: @free
CHECK-NOT: memcpy

// and no call at all - `reserve`, the element appends, the enum's teardown and the array's are inlined
// away, which is the stronger statement: a body LLVM could delete an allocation out of is one it had
// already seen every use of
CHECK-NOT: call
CHECK: ret i64
